  "content": {
    "title": "Where is Kid Rock's 'Southern White House' in Nashville? What to know",
    "text": "April 1, 2026, 3:22 p.m. CTThe Kid Rock Apache helicopter controversy came to a close on March 31 after Secretary of War Pete Hegseth lifted the suspensions of the pilots who visited the musician's home on March 28.\"No punishment. No investigation,\" wrote Hegseth in his post announcing the lifted suspensions.\"Carry on, patriots,\" he concluded.Prior to the announcement, a U.S. official who spoke on condition of anonymity told Reuters that the Army suspended the aircrew of the two Apache attack helicopters from Fort Campbell. The suspensions followed a video posted by Kid Rock showing the helicopters hover near his Nashville home, labeled the \"Southern White House\".Where is Kid Rock's 'Southern White House'?Kid Rock's \"Southern White House\" is located atop a hill in Whites Creek, a suburb north of Nashville. The 27,000-square-foot replica of the White House sits on substantial piece of property that has a church, a barber shop, and a gas station. Kid Rock reportedly refers to the house and the greater property as a \"Redneck Paradise,\" according to a 2022 Tucker Carlson Fox News segment.Located roughly 15-20 minutes north of downtown Nashville, Whites Creek is a historic rural community in Davidson County. The neighborhood has long been valued for its open land and privacy, as properties often sit on multiple acres and are far off the road behind tree lines.When did Kid Rock purchase the property and how big is it?In 2015, Kid Rock bought 102 acres in Whites Creek for $800,000, according to previous Tennessean reporting. Prior to that purchase, the musician built his multimillion-dollar home on 68 acres nearby.\"He plans to use it as a backyard,\" seller William A. Reynolds told the Tennessean in 2015 regarding the purchase. Kid Rock reportedly bought six more acres nearby, making the estimated acreage 176.Kid Rock has been a Nashville-resident since 2005.What has Kid Rock said about his 'Southern White House' and White Creek property?In the 2022 interview with Tucker Carlson, Kid Rock took the former Fox News anchor on a tour of the property and told him that he'd been \"dreaming it up for 20 years.\" Subsequently, he told Carlson an anecdote of when he first found the rural property, which included trekking through the woods until he came across the view seen in the viral helicopter video.\"Write them a check,\" Kid Rock said.Peter Burditt covers trending news and service journalism for The Tennessean. Contact him at PBurditt@nashvill.gannett.com",
